-- title:
--   Gaussian bound for the endpoint error of the smooth truncation
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathrm{endpointError}(r,t)=\mathrm{errorProfile}(t/r)/t$, where the error profile is the difference between the smooth kernel profile and the sharp step $\kappa_0\mathbf 1_{|v|>1}$. For $r>0$ and all $t$,
--   $$
--   \bigl|\mathrm{endpointError}(r,t)\bigr|\le K_{\mathrm{env}}\,\phi_{6r^2}(t),
--   $$
--   where $K_{\mathrm{env}}$ is the envelope constant and $\phi_\sigma$ the centred Gaussian density of variance $\sigma$.
--
--   The error made by smoothing a sharp truncation at radius $r$ is a Gaussian bump at scale $r$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/TriangularHilbert/ErrorEnvelope.lean#L100-L112

